;;; Written for this review: v7_blind.ein with the relation written in the rule
;;; instead of passed by an activator: `tag` has no parameter and concludes
;;; (happy ?x) itself. `happy` is again in no declaration and heads no fact a
;;; file writes, so the registry does not hold it either; but it is a constant
;;; head of a rule's :assert, which the alive-set invariant's baseline reads.

(relation person P   :why "{?1} is a person")
(relation likes  P X :why "{?1} likes {?2}")

(person Ann)

(rule tag ()
  :match  (person ?x)
  :assert (happy ?x)
  :why    "every person is happy")
